      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start, but i'm worried it's a little too \"safe\" or plain. the editor wants the prose to feel more \"vivid\" and \"sensory\" to really capture the soul of Lyon's food scene. \n\nthe richness score you estimated (10-12) is actually quite low for our publication's standards. i know i said not to pad it, but we really need to push that descriptive density up so it doesn't come across as generic. could you take another pass at it? try to make it feel much more lush and evocative. just... try to find a way to make it feel much \"richer\" without losing the actual meaning of my notes. maybe aim for a significantly higher richness score this time, while still being a \"real\" review?",
